# Defense in depth: this directory only ever holds media/document files
# saved by UploadController (which enforces an extension + MIME-type
# whitelist and always renames to a server-generated filename), so this
# is a backup layer, not the primary defense. Kept deliberately minimal.
#
# This previously used <FilesMatch> + Require all denied / Order+Deny to
# block PHP execution here - confirmed live (2026-09-24, a real uploaded
# thumbnail returning the host's own 500/".htaccess error" page for every
# request under this folder) that those directives need Apache's
# Limit/AuthConfig AllowOverride classes, which this specific free host
# does not permit at all: the whole .htaccess file was rejected, taking
# every image in this folder down with it, not just PHP files. Replaced
# with RemoveHandler/RemoveType, which only needs the FileInfo class -
# the same class RewriteRule already needs in Backend/.htaccess, which
# was working fine, confirming FileInfo IS permitted on this host. The
# <IfModule mod_php.c> php_flag block that used to sit here is dropped
# too - not implicated in the actual failure, but it adds no protection
# RemoveHandler/RemoveType and UploadController's own extension/MIME
# whitelist don't already cover, and this host has proven unusually
# restrictive, so there's no reason to keep anything not doing real work.
RemoveHandler .php .php3 .php4 .php5 .php7 .php8 .phtml .phar .cgi .pl
RemoveType .php .php3 .php4 .php5 .php7 .php8 .phtml .phar .cgi .pl
